{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jburlnnlsylrnohn7tvv6piaahr3nftp2tpn3hlz7q3tc4zyh5ja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The complete C library is translated and verified.\n\n## What was in scope\n`c_src/` is a small cute_c2-style 2D raycast library (1 source file, 321 lines) that CMake globs into one shared lib. `nm -D` on the C `.so` exports **22 public symbols** — no namespace/renaming macros in `lib.h`, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Deliverables\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, lib name `translated_rust` (matches the name CMake derives for the C lib)\n- `src/lib.rs` — all 22 exports as `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`, with `repr(C)` structs (`c2v`, `c2Raycast`, `c2Circle`, `c2AABB`, `c2Capsule`, `c2Ray`, `c2m`) so struct-by-value passing/returning matches the SysV classification the C uses.\n\n## Completion gate: symbol diff is empty\n`diff` of the two `nm -D` lists → **IDENTICAL: 22 symbols, zero difference** (`c2V c2Dot c2Len c2Add c2Sub c2Mulvs c2Div c2Norm c2Minv c2Maxv c2Skew c2Absv c2CCW90 c2MulmvT c2AABBtoAABB c2AABBtoPoint c2CircleToPoint c2RaytoCircle c2RaytoAABB c2RaytoCapsule c2CastRay spec_ray`). No extra exports, no missing ones. The `static inline` helpers stay private, as in C.\n\n## Bit-exactness verified (not just compiling)\nI wrote a `dlopen` harness that calls all 22 functions in both `.so`s and `memcmp`s return values and out-params. Against **both** `-O0` and `-O2` C builds:\n- 10.8M checks, finite inputs → **0 mismatches**\n- 10.8M checks with infinities → **0 mismatches**\n- 1M NaN/Inf-heavy `spec_ray` calls (the only function in the public header) → **0 mismatches**\n\nFidelity details that mattered: ternary `min`/`max`/`abs` were kept as literal ternaries (not `f32::min`/`abs`, which differ on `-0.0` and NaN); `c2Div` multiplies by `1.0f/b`; no bug fixes — the premature `out->n`/`out->t` writes in `c2RaytoCapsule`, the thrice-recomputed dot product in `c2RaytoAABB`, and the dead `return 0` in `c2CastRay` are preserved.\n\n## One honest caveat\nFeeding raw NaN *bit patterns* directly into the low-level vector functions yields NaN-**payload** differences (142 of 8.1M checks). This is not a translation defect: the two C builds of the identical source disagree with each other on 160 such checks, because payload propagation depends on which register `addss`/`mulss` uses as destination. I tested two mitigations — source-level operand swapping (142→124) and disabling SLP vectorization (142→137) — neither meaningfully converges, and both are LLVM-scheduling artifacts, so I kept the faithful default build rather than adding non-portable flags. Every generated NaN (default `0x7fc00000`), all infinities, signed zeros, and `spec_ray` under NaN input are exact."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":622,"cache_read_input_tokens":57900,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":622,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"540ac2e0-43b4-4046-9759-052d9c4f4812","uuid":"befb691d-fb78-40e0-a833-9b199a48a6e7","timestamp":"2026-08-20T05:04:09.759Z"}
